I found another option that works pretty well. It turns out if you plot the images using plotRefToTarget as usual and then save the images using pdf(), R will produce an image with a clipping mask around it that work pretty well in keeping the overall size of the plots the same even if one is very long in the x-axis and the other is long in the y-axis. Removing the clipping mask can be a bit of a pain due to how Adobe Illustrator interprets the files, but it is possible and it is nice for keeping plot outputs at a comparable size within a figure.

